// DO NOT add a mypy-restart keybinding to this file.
//
// A chord binding "mypy-type-checker.restart" was removed from all three
// repositories. It shipped, it was "fixed" twice, and it never worked. The
// reasons, in order of discovery:
//
//  1. It was gated on `"when": "editorTextFocus || terminalFocus"`, which is
//     false whenever you are reading the PROBLEMS PANEL - the one place you
//     are when stale diagnostics are what you need to clear. A false `when`
//     clause disables a key silently: no error, and no conflict in Ctrl+K
//     Ctrl+S. Removing it did not fix the problem.
//
//  2. With no `when` clause it became a valid, unconditional binding, and it
//     STILL did nothing. The extension logs show it activates only on
//     'onLanguage:python', and its own restart path short-circuits when it is
//     not holding a live server session:
//
//         if (S = [], y) return;
//
//     It returns silently - no error, no notification - so the command runs
//     and no-ops. Restarting is only meaningful when a server is already
//     running for the file you have open.
//
// The real trigger, from the extension's own log, is 'textDocument/didOpen':
//
//     textDocument/didOpen
//     textDocument/didOpen
//
// So the reliable refresh is to CLOSE THE FILE AND OPEN IT AGAIN. That fires
// didOpen, which re-runs mypy against the current bytes on disk.
//
// If that is inconvenient, from the repo root:
//
//     uv run python .github/scripts/refresh_editor_types.py
//
// which nudges a tracked setting to prompt the same re-check and needs no
// keybinding. Note the explicit `uv run`: this repository has no bare
// `python` on PATH, so a bare `python ...` fails with *command not found*.
//
// Do not re-add a keybinding here without reading this first.
[]
